--
N5008 [dcl.typedef]/2, [temp.variadic]/5: for X<int, char>, `using F =
void(T...);' is void(int, char).  Assigning cb to the F * member was a
conversion error ("invalid implicit conversion from 'auto (*)(signed int,
char) -> void' to 'auto (*)(signed int) -> void'", bin53): when the class
body is substituted (template_mapt::apply), class packs are expanded in the
function types of member declarators, but an alias-declaration carries its
function type in the declaration's type (merged with the typedef
specifier), so the pack was substituted by its first element.
`typedef void F(T...);' worked.  test_shapes.desc: other packs and
patterns.  g++ 13
and clang++ 18 accept this program, and it fails only its WRONG assertion.
